<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Direct (Developer ID) build. One entitlement, for one module.

	Hardened Runtime is on, the sandbox is off, and the app itself needs
	nothing: reading ~/.claude is plain filesystem access, and the hook bridge
	listens on 127.0.0.1 which is unrestricted outside the sandbox.

	audio-input is for the Warm Microphone module. Under the hardened runtime
	macOS refuses the microphone to an app without it, before the user is even
	asked. The module is off until installed, and nothing else opens a
	microphone.

	Do not add com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation or any JIT /
	unsigned-memory exception here. They weaken the runtime and docs/06 says we
	have no concrete need for one.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
